From d5df73af745f6fc2a4d113ca3086e8c2a16c7b10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nake Sekander <nake.sekander@strakergroup.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 11:16:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] fix(agent): behaviour changes from the mock-up review

First-person voice in conversation, never 'we'. Two plans: a request and its
execution are separate streamed messages, because Slack attaches buttons only
when a stream ends. No task card for simple look-ups. Approval is never a task
and a declined step is removed, not marked done. AI disclaimer only on replies
that deliver AI output. Suggestions go by direct message and say that inline
translation is metered. Stop keeps approved, paid work running.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
